{"kosher":{"id":"fa83bae9-667b-4e74-9f86-1f8e1068edbb","word":"kosher","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"in accordance with Jewish law","word":"kosher"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Only in New York can you find a good, kosher hamburger!","bold_text_offsets":[[38,44]],"type":"example","id":"92e2b872-e933-4175-8955-464f6daf806b"},{"text":"David's mother kept a kosher kitchen, with separate sets of dishes for meat and for dairy.","bold_text_offsets":[[22,28]],"type":"example","id":"23d12d41-7301-450f-a3a1-eede4fae2cfb"},{"text":"In order for a suit to be kosher, it cannot contain both wool and linen together.","bold_text_offsets":[[26,32]],"type":"example","id":"53947e15-873b-4921-8cef-4bc4a2627098"},{"text":"Admirers of Israel’s kosher and nonkosher wines need the 2007 edition of “Rogov’s Guide to Israeli Wines” (Toby Press, $19.95).","ref":"2007 January 14, Howard G. Goldberg, “A Tour of Israel, Bottle by Bottle”, in The New York Times, archived from the original on 30 Jun 2013:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[21,27],[35,41]],"id":"e808a81b-42bb-44ed-a701-7d2bef11089d"}],"senseid":["en:in accordance with Jewish law"],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples","en:Judaism"],"links":[["Judaism","Judaism"],["consumption","consumption"],["Jewish","Jewish"],["law","law"]],"hypernyms":[{"word":"allowable"},{"word":"abideable","source":"Thesaurus:permissible"},{"word":"acceptable","source":"Thesaurus:permissible"},{"word":"admissible","source":"Thesaurus:permissible"},{"word":"allowable","source":"Thesaurus:permissible"},{"word":"permissible","source":"Thesaurus:permissible"},{"word":"sufferable","source":"Thesaurus:permissible"},{"word":"supportable","source":"Thesaurus:permissible"},{"word":"tolerable","source":"Thesaurus:permissible"}],"raw_glosses":["(Judaism) Fit for use or consumption, in accordance with Jewish law (especially relating to food)."],"glosses":["Fit for use or consumption, in accordance with Jewish law (especially relating to food)."],"tags":["Judaism"],"id":"4d75840d-6afb-457f-b04d-fd862ab7523f"},{"examples":[{"text":"\"Are you kosher?\" \"No, I love to eat scallops.\"","bold_text_offsets":[[9,15]],"type":"example","id":"93549219-c232-4d53-9e92-f2151c0ed84c"},{"text":"\"Is this restaurant kosher?\" \"No, we serve pork.\"","bold_text_offsets":[[20,26]],"type":"example","id":"07afb4da-82b7-4f11-af51-8aee4cdd3c39"}],"links":[["Observant","observant"],["kashrut","kashrut"]],"glosses":["Observant of the rules of kashrut (of a person or establishment)."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"id":"f74d6e5a-0df3-41ca-8146-52a8182e5a42"},{"examples":[{"text":"Is what I have done kosher with Mr. Smith?","bold_text_offsets":[[20,26]],"type":"example","id":"30bdea27-6523-4242-81d2-70a265302d27"}],"senseid":["en:figuratively, normal or standard"],"links":[["standard","standard"],["usual","usual"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"by the book"},{"word":"proper"},{"word":"rightful"},{"word":"halal","source":"Thesaurus:orthodox","tags":["figuratively"]},{"word":"homodox","source":"Thesaurus:orthodox","tags":["uncommon"]},{"word":"kosher","source":"Thesaurus:orthodox","tags":["figuratively"]},{"word":"orthodox","source":"Thesaurus:orthodox"},{"word":"by the book","source":"Thesaurus:orthodox"},{"word":"allowed","source":"Thesaurus:orthodox"},{"word":"conventional","source":"Thesaurus:orthodox"},{"word":"customary","source":"Thesaurus:orthodox"},{"word":"natural","source":"Thesaurus:orthodox"},{"word":"official","source":"Thesaurus:orthodox"},{"word":"proper","source":"Thesaurus:orthodox"},{"word":"routine","source":"Thesaurus:orthodox"},{"word":"traditional","source":"Thesaurus:orthodox"}],"raw_glosses":["(figuratively, by extension) In accordance with standards or usual practice."],"glosses":["In accordance with standards or usual practice."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"tags":["broadly","figuratively"],"id":"8725e8d3-36d8-4d7c-b49f-7ad9d62e273e"}],"related":[{"word":"kasher"},{"word":"kashrut"}],"synonyms":[]},"kosovo":{"id":"f56c4f76-5b76-4714-9dff-a0e44fd4f0ab","word":"Kosovo","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"disputed region in the Balkans","tags":["masculine"],"word":"Cosovo"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"disputed region in the Balkans","tags":["masculine"],"word":"Kosovo"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Yugoslavia’s President, Slobodan Milosevic, has rejected all efforts at meaningful diplomacy and, in violation of his own previous commitments, has ratcheted up his military campaign against the innocent civilians of Kosovo.","ref":"1999 March 25, “Air Campaign Against Yugoslavia”, in The New York Times, New York:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[217,223]],"id":"fe22bf5a-87a1-4864-82f2-0cdeeeb90e21"},{"text":"After Milosevic’s overthrow in October 2000, international pressure on the new authorities in Belgrade to extradict Milosevic for alleged war crimes committed during the Kosovo conflict was intense.","ref":"2017, Freedom in the world, page 657:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[170,176]],"id":"93e30fdf-90e9-4c61-8bb6-f7c21119114d"},{"text":"A prominent Kosovo Serb politician, Oliver Ivanovic, was shot dead outside his party offices Tuesday morning, halting talks between Kosovar and Serb delegates that had been set to resume that day.","ref":"2018 January 16, Milena Veselinovic and Sheena McKenzie, “Leading Kosovo Serb politician Oliver Ivanovic shot dead outside office”, in CNN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[12,18]],"id":"1c4885c2-5888-4cdd-8b67-d678ed3136e1"}],"wikidata":["Q1246"],"senseid":["en:Q1246"],"categories":["English terms with quotations","en:Countries in Europe","en:Kosovo"],"links":[["country","country"],["Balkan Peninsula","Balkan Peninsula#English"],["Southeast Europe","Southeast Europe#English"],["Republic of Kosovo","Republic of Kosovo#English"],["Pristina","Pristina#English"],["Republic of Serbia","Republic of Serbia"]],"glosses":["A partly-recognized country on the Balkan Peninsula in Southeast Europe. Official name: Republic of Kosovo. Capital and largest city: Pristina. Considered by the Republic of Serbia to be one of its two autonomous provinces."],"id":"b79c600c-0f2d-4605-94b7-d087225f5b59"},{"glosses":["One of five administrative districts of the above region as viewed by the Serbian government."],"id":"fa63dc01-f542-450e-8458-7f3366175c7d"}],"related":[{"word":"Kosovo and Metohia"}],"synonyms":[]},"kos":{"id":"8349fc42-1891-405a-9f5f-c8de19c30784","word":"Kos","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"island","word":"Cós"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"categories":["English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English proper nouns","English terms borrowed from Ancient Greek","English terms borrowed from Greek","English terms derived from Ancient Greek","English terms derived from Greek","English uncountable nouns","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 8 entries","Pages with entries","Terms with Ancient Greek translations","Terms with Arabic translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with Greek translations","Terms with Hijazi Arabic translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Japanese translations","Terms with Latin translations","Terms with Ottoman Turkish translations","Terms with Persian translations","Terms with Polish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Turkish translations","en:Islands","en:Places in Greece"],"links":[["island","island"],["Dodecanese","Dodecanese#English"],["Greece","Greece#English"]],"glosses":["An island of the Dodecanese, Greece."],"id":"7cd087f7-a867-4290-a2cb-e186a5a78ad7"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"kosovan":{"id":"c3591bf4-4f55-4289-bde3-cf8275ac70f3","word":"Kosovan","trans":[{"lang"